@@ -877,17 +881,34 @@ public final class AXWindowSystem: WindowSystem {
     knocks.knock(at: pid) { [weak self] attends in self?.doorOpens(of: pid, attends: attends) }
   }
 
+  /// Waits for the app on this thread, as everything about it used to be waited for, and serves what is behind its door. For the one case where
+  /// nothing else will do: the keyboard of the app in front is with a window that nobody has been told of (a new window, tab or dialog, a tab
+  /// that was chosen), or Arbor has never heard where it is. The next key is meant for that window. It cannot be answered before Arbor
+  /// has read what the app lists, and what waits here must not be overtaken by it: the window would be named to a controller that has not heard of it.
+  /// So this is called in the report's own turn of the run loop, never from within a command, and the key waits its turn. One timeout at most.
+  private func waitAtTheDoor(of pid: pid_t) {
+    // A new window is reported three times over: created, the keyboard, the main window. One timeout is paid for an app that hangs, not three. And of one
+    // that is busy moving its windows nothing is read when it does attend (`act`), so there is nothing to wait for.
+    guard answers(pid) else { return }
+    // Behind the knock, on the same queue. Whatever it says late is of no use: an app that let this go by is on record, and is asked until it wakes.
